[h1]Replimat Mech[/h1]
[i]A fork of [url=https://steamcommunity.com/sharedfiles/filedetails/?id=1715402900]Replimat[/url] by Robin "sumghai" Chang and Dubwise56 and [url=https://steamcommunity.com/sharedfiles/filedetails/?id=3806650178]Replimat Universal[/url] by Omnot. Unofficial; not endorsed by the original authors.[/i]

A copier for your colony's production.
The splitter works like a crematorium: by its bills it splits items and corpses into matter (mass and value) and records their patterns.
Replicators work like workbenches: by their bills they print from those patterns, paying time, mass and value.
The links of the computer operator (replink, mechlink, biolink) set what prints and how fast.
Mechanoids are printed like in a gestator, and resurrected.
[b]New in 1.2:[/b] bioreplication — adult tame animals by DNA and colonists by templates.

[b]Incompatible with Replimat and Replimat Universal.[/b]

[img]https://raw.githubusercontent.com/ivni77/Replimat-Mech/main/Workshop/Images/1.jpg[/img]

[h2]Features[/h2]
[list]
[*][b]Splitter[/b]: crematorium-style bills (filter, hit points, quality); the pattern is recorded at the best quality seen. Corpses split without mood penalties. [b]Scan[/b] has one piece brought in.
[*][b]Tanks[/b] store mass up to capacity and value without limit, shared across the network; the large one holds four times more.
[*][b]Replicators[/b] (standing and wall) print in batches of up to a stack. The [b]animal replicator[/b] prints feed into itself.
[*][b]Bills[/b] like a workbench: all three modes, pause, reorder, copy and paste. [b]Surplus[/b]: haulers take the excess to the splitter.
[*][b]Operator and links[/b]: a colonist with a link contacts the computer once. Replink: items; vanilla mechlink: mechs, chips, subcores; biolink: bioreplication. Replink and biolink level up from the value printed, up to 175% speed.
[*][b]Mechs[/b]: mechanitor and control group per bill; corpses are resurrected in the replicator.
[*][b]Bioscanner[/b]: records the DNA of a living animal or person, unharmed (or of a fresh corpse in the splitter). The [b]bioreplicator[/b] grows from matter, no food, an adult tame animal (female or male) or a colonist by template.
[*][b]People[/b]: templates built from blocks — appearance, skills, passions, up to three traits, genes; scanned people add their traits and genes. Printed colonists are 18, without relatives; no randomness.
[*][b]Trash[/b]: whatever you delete from the print lists can be restored from it.
[*][b]Computer window[/b]: matter, buildings, links, all bills.
[*][b]Sliders[/b]: print faster for more value or cheaper for more time, up to 40%.
[*][b]Only researched things are printed[/b], like vanilla. Deleting a bill returns the unprinted batch to the tanks.
[*]Exotic goods traders sell replimat buildings.
[/list]

[img]https://raw.githubusercontent.com/ivni77/Replimat-Mech/main/Workshop/Images/2.png[/img]
[img]https://raw.githubusercontent.com/ivni77/Replimat-Mech/main/Workshop/Images/3.png[/img]
