[h2]Quick start[/h2]
[olist]
[*]Research [b]Replication[/b].
[*]On one power network build a [b]computer[/b], [b]tanks[/b], a [b]splitter[/b] and a [b]replicator[/b].
[*]Make a [b]replink[/b] at a machining table and install it (a mechanitor can use the mechlink alone).
[*]Right-click the computer with that colonist: [b]Contact the computer[/b].
[*]Add bills to the splitter (or use [b]Scan[/b]) and to the replicator.
[/olist]

[img]https://raw.githubusercontent.com/ivni77/Replimat-Mech/main/Workshop/Images/6.png[/img]

[h2]Settings[/h2]
Mass and value collected on splitting (value 5–60%, so print-and-split never profits), color, print quality cap, special items and bioreplication (allow, markup), movable tanks, tank capacity, power use.
Stored value adds to colony wealth; [b]Collect value[/b] in the computer window turns it off.

[h2]Compatibility[/h2]
RimWorld [b]1.6[/b]. Requires [url=https://steamcommunity.com/sharedfiles/filedetails/?id=2009463077]Harmony[/url] and [b]Biotech[/b]. Languages: English, Russian.
Works with [url=https://steamcommunity.com/sharedfiles/filedetails/?id=2606448745]Multiplayer[/url]: edits are synced. Mod settings must match the host: change them before joining, a change during the game desyncs.

